
.databricks

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local MLflow tracking store created by era/tests. Per-machine state, not
# project code - the donor repo committed one of these by accident.
mlflow.db
mlruns/

# Corpus documents built by the scripts in resources/. Roughly 30 MB of PDF that
# is fully reproducible from conf/companies.yaml:
#   resources/fetch_filings.py          -> data/edgar_10k, data/edgar_10q
#   resources/generate_synthetic_docs.py -> data/synthetic
# The Mag7 PDFs under data/10k, data/10Q and friends stay committed - they are the
# original corpus and there is no script that reproduces them.
#
# data/corpus_manifest.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it records exactly which
# filing (accession number, source URL, checksum) each document came from, and
# which documents are generated. That record is worth having in git even though
# the documents themselves are not.
data/edgar_10k/
data/edgar_10q/
data/synthetic/

# Mirrored Databricks AI Dev Kit installs for other assistants. The lockfile
# (skills-lock.json) is the source of truth; regenerate rather than committing
# ~16 MB of duplicated trees. Keep .claude/ for this project's own skills.
.gemini/
.windsurf/
.kiro/
.opencode/
.agents/
.ai-dev-kit/
.github/skills/
